  "answer": "I don't have a shell tool to run tests, so I'll verify the logic by careful reasoning against each requirement:\n\n**Validation** — `ranges` must be an array (else `TypeError`); each element must be a 2-element array; both bounds must be `Number.isSafeInteger`; `start <= end`. All violations throw `TypeError`. ✓\n\n**No mutation** — I build a fresh `pairs` array of fresh `[start, end]` copies via `.map`, then sort that copy. The original array and its pairs are never touched. ✓\n\n**Sort** — by start, then end (`a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]`). ✓\n\n**Merge with adjacency** — `start <= last[1] + 1` merges overlapping *and* touching intervals (`[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`). ✓\n\n**Contained intervals** — only extend when `end > last[1]`, so a contained interval never shortens the current one. ✓\n\n**Fresh output** — result holds newly created `[start, end]` arrays inside a fresh array. ✓\n\n**Empty input** — `[]` maps to `[]`, loop produces `[]`. ✓\n\n**Named export** — `export function mergeRanges` preserved. ✓\n\nLet me trace the two provided tests:\n\n- `[[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]]` → sorted `[[1,3],[2,5],[8,10]]` → `[1,3]`; `2 <= 4` → extend to `[1,5]`; `8 <= 6`? no → push `[8,10]` → `[[1,5],[8,10]]` ✓\n- `[[5,7],[2,4]]` → sorted `[[2,4],[5,7]]` → `5 <= 5` → extend to `[2,7]` → `[[2,7]]` ✓\n\nBoth match the expected outputs.\n\n## Summary\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges` in `ranges.mjs` to fully meet the spec:\n\n- **Strict validation**: throws `TypeError` for non-array input, non-pair elements, non-safe-integer bounds, or `start > end`.\n- **No mutation**: copies each pair into a fresh array before sorting, leaving the input and its pairs untouched.\n- **Correct ordering**: sorts by start, then end.\n- **Adjacency-aware merging**: uses `start <= last[1] + 1` so overlapping *and* touching integer intervals merge.\n- **Contained intervals preserved**: only extends the current interval when `end > last[1]`.\n- **Fresh output**: returns new pair arrays in a new result array; empty input returns `[]`.\n- **Named export** kept intact.\n\nNote: I attempted to add extra edge-case tests to `public.test.mjs`, but that file is not writable (permission denied), so it remains unchanged. The implementation passes both existing tests by trace-through.",
